---
/**
 * Override of @astrojs/starlight/components/TwoColumnContent.astro.
 *
 * Starlight's default reserves a right-hand column here (`.right-sidebar-
 * container`, sized off `--sl-sidebar-width`) whenever the page has a TOC
 * at all, regardless of what `PageSidebar` actually renders into it. This
 * site's `PageSidebar` override no longer puts a desktop panel there (see
 * that file), but the page still carries `toc` data — it's needed for the
 * mobile TOC bar and for the TOC now embedded in the left `Sidebar` — so
 * `data-has-toc` stays set and the default would keep reserving that empty
 * column, pushing the content off-centre to the left.
 *
 * This override drops the reserved column and its width/margin math
 * entirely, letting `.main-pane` take the full remaining width so
 * `ContentPanel`'s own `margin-inline: auto` centres the content measure
 * normally in the space left after the (still present) left sidebar.
 * `--sl-content-width` (the actual text measure) is untouched — this only
 * changes what surrounds it, not its size, per the instruction not to
 * widen the content column.
 *
 * `<slot name="right-sidebar" />` is still rendered (unwrapped, with no
 * width reserved) so `PageSidebar`'s mobile TOC — which positions itself
 * with `position: fixed` and doesn't depend on its layout parent — still
 * ends up in the DOM.
 */
---

<div class="lg:sl-flex">
	<slot name="right-sidebar" />
	<div class="main-pane"><slot /></div>
</div>

<style>
	@layer starlight.core {
		.main-pane {
			isolation: isolate;
			width: 100%;
		}
	}
</style>
